WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:44.631 --> 00:00:46.830
[Narrator] This is Horiyoshi III,

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:50.362
one of the world's most legendary
full-body-tattoo artists.

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:54.490
His given name is Yoshihito Nakano,

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:57.180
but he inherited the title Horiyoshi,

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:59.250
which is derived from the word "hori,"

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:02.130
meaning "to carve or engrave."

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:04.526
This is his studio, hidden away

00:01:04.526 --> 00:01:08.400
in an anonymous-looking building
in the city of Yokohama,

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.681
a 30-minute train ride from Tokyo.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:34.970
The controversial history of
Japanese tattooing, or irezumi,

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:39.970
can be traced back to around
10,000 BC, in the Jomon period.

00:01:39.972 --> 00:01:43.720
The Japanese government
banned tattoos in 1872,

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:46.370
as while the practice
had risen as an art form,

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:49.685
tattooed marks were still
used as a punishment.

00:01:49.685 --> 00:01:52.900
The ban wasn't lifted until 1948,

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:56.380
but the practice has retained
its image of criminality.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:59.120
For many years, traditional
Japanese tattoos

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:02.760
were associated with the
yakuza, Japan's Mafia,

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:05.470
and some businesses in
Japan and public baths

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:07.393
still ban tattooed customers.

00:03:35.998 --> 00:03:38.542
Yoshihito's most devoted clientele

00:03:38.542 --> 00:03:41.170
are covered in full-body designs.

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:43.900
These stop sharply at the wrist and ankle,

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:46.981
where skin would show when
wearing a traditional kimono.

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:53.360
There's also the hikae,
a chest panel to sleeve,

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:56.370
nagasode, a full sleeve to the wrist,

00:03:56.370 --> 00:04:00.249
and shorter sleeves, shichibu and gobu.

00:04:00.249 --> 00:04:03.810
Donburi soshinbori is a full-body tattoo

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:06.152
without the line down
the center of the chest.

00:06:16.526 --> 00:06:18.157
Until 30 years ago,

00:06:18.157 --> 00:06:21.260
Yoshihito did his tattoos entirely by hand

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:23.730
using the tebori technique,

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:26.210
where a needle-tipped
wooden or metal stick

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:28.315
inserts ink into the skin.

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:32.740
Nowadays, due to health
and time constraints,

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:36.167
he completes them freehand
using an electric needle.

00:07:45.458 --> 00:07:47.742
Yoshihito wants to keep the traditional

00:07:47.742 --> 00:07:50.623
generational structure of the Horiyoshi.

00:08:03.298 --> 00:08:05.650
The majority of Yoshihito's clients

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:07.500
are now foreign visitors,

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:10.300
and he has a large international
following on Instagram.

00:08:11.210 --> 00:08:15.002
A tattoo in Japan costs
up to 15,000 yen per hour,

00:08:15.002 --> 00:08:17.109
or $140,

00:08:17.109 --> 00:08:20.370
but Yoshihito's designs
are more expensive.

